Send no HEVC entry point count

GStreamer's vah265dec decoded nothing. Every picture failed with
vaEndPicture -> DECODING_ERROR and zero VE interrupts, while the kernel
logged

  cedrus 1c0e000.video-codec: Failed to setup decoding job: -34

-ERANGE is cedrus_h265_setup's check that num_entry_point_offsets equals
the length of the V4L2_CID_STATELESS_HEVC_ENTRY_POINT_OFFSETS array.
VA-API carries the entry point count in VASliceParameterBufferHEVC but
not the offsets, so this driver never sends that array, and any non-zero
count is refused.

ffmpeg never fills num_entry_point_offsets (libavcodec/vaapi_hevc.c, 7.1),
so its slices always arrived with 0 and decode bit-exact; that is the
path the HEVC gate validates. GStreamer (gstvah265dec.c, 1.26.2) copies
the slice header's count, which is non-zero for any WPP or tiled stream.
Send 0 whatever the client says, which is what the validated path
already sends.

---
diff --git a/src/h265.c b/src/h265.c
index e0838a6..87eb5f1 100644
--- a/src/h265.c
+++ b/src/h265.c
@@ -349,7 +349,19 @@ static void h265_fill_slice_params(VAPictureParameterBufferHEVC *picture,
 	/* DBO_EXPERIMENT */
 	slice_params->data_byte_offset =
 		slice->slice_data_offset + slice->slice_data_byte_offset;
-	slice_params->num_entry_point_offsets = slice->num_entry_point_offsets;
+	/*
+	 * Always 0. VA-API carries the entry point COUNT in the slice
+	 * parameters but not the offsets, so the
+	 * V4L2_CID_STATELESS_HEVC_ENTRY_POINT_OFFSETS array is never sent, and
+	 * cedrus refuses a slice whose count differs from the array it got
+	 * (-ERANGE in cedrus_h265_setup, before the engine runs). ffmpeg never
+	 * fills the field, so its slices arrive with 0 and decode bit-exact --
+	 * that is the path the HEVC gate validates. GStreamer's vah265dec copies
+	 * the slice header's num_entry_point_offsets, and every one of its
+	 * WPP/tiled slices was refused: "Failed to setup decoding job: -34",
+	 * vaEndPicture -> DECODING_ERROR, zero VE interrupts.
+	 */
+	slice_params->num_entry_point_offsets = 0;
 	slice_params->nal_unit_type = nal_unit_type;
 	slice_params->nuh_temporal_id_plus1 = nuh_temporal_id_plus1;
 
